/-!
# Classification of continuous one-parameter subgroups

This file proves that every continuous homomorphism from the real line to a finite-dimensional Lie
group is generated by a unique tangent vector, equivalently by a unique left-invariant derivation.
The proof uses a private dyadic-local-logarithm argument: logarithms at dyadic times converge to
zero, eventually scale exactly under time halving, and therefore determine one global generator.

## Main results

* `existsUnique_eq_mulInvariantOneParameterSubgroup`: tangent-vector existence and uniqueness.
* `oneParameterSubgroupEquiv`: the classification equivalence between left-invariant derivations and
  continuous one-parameter subgroups.
* `existsUnique_eq_oneParameterSubgroup`: the derivation-based existence-and-uniqueness statement.

## References

* [Lie groups and the Lie algebra correspondence roadmap](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiRoadmap/blob/main/TauCetiRoadmap/RepresentationTheory/LieGroups/README.md),
  Deliverable A, Layer 0, "One-parameter subgroups".
-/

public section

open Filter Function Manifold Set
open scoped ContDiff Manifold Topology

noncomputable section

/-- The dyadic time step `2⁻ⁿ`. -/
private def dyadicStep (n : ℕ) : ℝ := (2 : ℝ)⁻¹ ^ n

variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]
  {H : Type*} [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H}
  {G : Type*} [TopologicalSpace G] [ChartedSpace H G] [Group G]
  [IsManifold I 1 G]

attribute [local instance] LieGroup.minSmoothnessThree
